Help Desk & IT Support Lab

This will be a simulated help desk environment that will cover many scenarios that may come in the field. Scenarios such as ticket resolution, user/access management, trouble shooting, remote support, and machine deployment. This lab is meant to mirror Tier 1 help desk support roles 

**AD LAB**
Active Directory environment (Windows Server + AD DS) will simulate user lifecycle mangement: onboarding/offboarding, OU structure, group policy, permissions
troubleshooting, and account recovery.
- Status: In progress
- Tools: Windows Server 2022, AD DS, GPO, VirtualBox

**TICKETING SYSTEM** 
Self-hosted ticketing system (osTicket) with realistic support tickets that will cover hardware, software, network, and access categories. Includes triage
priority logic and resolution documentation.
- Status: Not started
- Tools: osTicket

**RUNBOOK** 
Diagnostic runbook for common end-user issues — symptom-based troubleshooting
trees for boot failures, network drops, printing, blue screens, performance,
login issues, and software crashes.
- Status: In progress
- Format: Markdown, one doc per symptom category

**REMOTE SUPPORT**

Recorded/documented remote troubleshooting sessions simulating real support
calls using remote desktop tooling.
- Status: Not started
- Tools: TeamViewer / RDP

**IMAGING**
Machine imaging and deployment workflow — capturing, restoring, and deploying
a standard OS image across VMs.
- Status: Not started
- Tools: Clonezilla
